<section class="home-block home-block--paper" id="how-it-works">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="section__head">
				<p>Leasing Tips</p>
				<h2>Tenants</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="probate-intro">
        	<p class="leasing-tips__lead">    
				<p>Entering into a commercial or retail lease is a significant financial and legal commitment. 
                   Before signing a lease, tenants should carefully consider the proposed terms, assess the commercial 
                   risks and obtain professional advice to protect their business interests. 
                   At Cleverminds Legal Centre, we assist tenants in understanding their obligations, protecting their 
                   interests and avoiding costly leasing disputes.</p>
                <br>
                <p> </p>
                   <p>
                   &nbsp;
                   </p>
			</div>
            
			<div class="instruments">
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">01</span>
					<h3>Understand Your Legal Obligations:</h3>
					<p>Carefully review all lease terms, conditions and financial commitments before signing any documents.</p>
                    </a>
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">02</span>
					<h3>Conduct Thorough Due Diligence:</h3>
					<p>Investigate the premises, location, surrounding businesses and potential risks before committing to a lease.</p>
					<!--- <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/power-of-attorney">Commercial Property Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">03</span>
					<h3>Assess Your Business Viability:</h3>
					<p>Prepare realistic financial forecasts covering expected sales, operating expenses, rental payments and business profitability.</p>
					<!--- <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Retirement Village Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">04</span>
					<h3>Negotiate Favourable Lease Terms:</h3>
					<p>Your strongest negotiating position is generally before signing the initial lease. Seek favourable terms from the outset.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Vacant Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">05</span>
					<h3>Consider Lease Renewal Options:</h3>
					<p>Where possible, negotiate an option to renew your lease to provide greater business certainty and protect your investment.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Rural Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">06</span>
					<h3>Protect Against Direct Competition:</h3>
					<p>Consider negotiating an exclusivity clause to restrict the landlord from leasing nearby premises to direct competitors.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Put & Call Options</a> --->
				</article>
                <article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">07</span>
					<h3>Document All Representations:</h3>
					<p>Ensure all promises and representations made by landlords or leasing agents are properly recorded in writing.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Vacant Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">08</span>
					<h3>Review Disclosure Statements Carefully:</h3>
					<p>Check that the disclosure documents accurately reflect the agreed terms and representations before signing.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Rural Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">09</span>
					<h3>Understand Personal Guarantees:</h3>
					<p>Carefully consider the financial risks of providing personal guarantees, which may expose your personal assets to liability.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Put & Call Options</a> --->
				</article>
                <article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">10</span>
					<h3>Compare Market Rental Rates:</h3>
					<p>Research comparable rental rates and available leasing incentives to determine whether the proposed rent is reasonable.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Put & Call Options</a> --->
				</article>
                <article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">11</span>
					<h3>Investigate Shopping Centre Performance:</h3>
					<p>Speak with existing tenants, assess customer traffic and investigate the commercial viability of the proposed location.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Vacant Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">12</span>
					<h3>Consider Fit-Out Costs:</h3>
					<p>Evaluate the costs of fitting out the premises and understand any obligations to remove fixtures or restore the premises when the lease ends.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Rural Land Sales</a> --->
				</article>
				<article class="instrument">
					<span class="instrument__num">13</span>
					<h3>Avoid Relying on Standard Lease Terms:</h3>
					<p>Do not assume a standard lease is fair or balanced. Lease agreements are frequently prepared to protect the landlord's interests.</p>
					<!---  <a class="instrument__link" href="/legal-services/enduring-guardian">Put & Call Options</a> --->
				</article>

			</div>
            
            <p>
               &nbsp;
            </p>
            <div class="probate-intro">
               <p class="leasing-tips__lead">    
				<p>At Cleverminds Legal Centre, our experienced leasing lawyers assist commercial and retail tenants with reviewing lease agreements, 
                negotiating favourable terms and understanding their legal obligations. We provide clear, practical legal advice to help tenants make 
                informed leasing decisions, minimise financial risks and protect their business interests.</p>
            </div>
		</div>
	</section>